  "term": "spatial frequency",
  "definition": "Spatial frequency is a visual property of a pattern, especially a grating, defined by the number of light-to-dark cycles across an area, often measured in cycles per degree of visual angle. Higher spatial frequencies correspond to finer local detail, whereas lower spatial frequencies correspond to coarser global information.",
